1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,528
Sound does not fade

2
00:00:01,528 --> 00:00:03,174
away smoothly. At the

3
00:00:03,174 --> 00:00:04,833
smallest scale, it jumps.

4
00:00:05,140 --> 00:00:06,738
Sound is vibration, and

5
00:00:06,738 --> 00:00:08,003
vibration is energy.

6
00:00:08,311 --> 00:00:09,650
At the quantum level

7
00:00:09,650 --> 00:00:10,989
that energy comes in

8
00:00:10,989 --> 00:00:12,439
packets called phonons.

9
00:00:12,746 --> 00:00:13,902
A phonon can only

10
00:00:13,902 --> 00:00:15,179
sit on fixed energy

11
00:00:15,179 --> 00:00:16,777
steps, never in between.

12
00:00:17,084 --> 00:00:18,866
Physicists at Stanford, in

13
00:00:18,866 --> 00:00:20,709
the Safavi-Naeini lab, built

14
00:00:20,709 --> 00:00:22,478
a tiny mechanical resonator

15
00:00:22,478 --> 00:00:23,818
that rings for about

16
00:00:23,818 --> 00:00:26,226
2 ms, and watched single

17
00:00:26,226 --> 00:00:27,934
phonons jump between those

18
00:00:27,934 --> 00:00:29,150
steps in real time.

19
00:00:29,458 --> 00:00:30,490
It is the first

20
00:00:30,490 --> 00:00:32,443
direct real-time observation of

21
00:00:32,443 --> 00:00:33,598
a quantum jump in

22
00:00:33,598 --> 00:00:35,491
sound. Quantum jumps were

23
00:00:35,491 --> 00:00:36,523
seen in ions in

24
00:00:36,523 --> 00:00:37,875
1986, in photons in

25
00:00:37,875 --> 00:00:39,423
2007, and now in sound.
